# KGB-CIA: every environment variable the pipeline can read, and the step that needs it.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored), fill in what you have, and run with
#     uv run --env-file .env <command>
# or export the variables from your shell or a secrets manager: scripts only read environment
# variables. Leave a line empty to use the default. Never commit a key.
#
# You need no key to build the graph (kgb-transform), clean it (kgb-clean), cut a subgraph
# (kgb-filter), or serve it (kgb-mcp). NodeNorm and PubMed are free and need no key either.
# Keys are only for the two steps that call a paid model: augmentation and the evidence check.

# --- Augmentation (kgb-augment): a language model, either of these ---------------------------
# Claude models, through Anthropic's API (`--model claude-...`). Your agent harness may read it
# too, if it is Claude Code or Pi with an Anthropic provider.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Azure OpenAI models (the default models). These are Pi's standard Azure names, so the Pi
# provider docs apply. The model ids in .pi/models.json are the project's own deployments: to
# use your own Azure OpenAI resource, set its endpoint here and deploy models under those ids.
# If you use Azure OpenAI for other work too, set these per project rather than globally.
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Empty: the project's endpoint. Yours looks like https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1
AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# --- Evidence check (evidence-check skill): TypeSafe AI's Jev model --------------------------
# Without it the skill writes the requests it would send and a cost estimate, and sends nothing.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- PubMed (augmentation and the evidence check), optional ----------------------------------
# NCBI allows 3 requests a second without a key and 10 with one. A key is free from an NCBI
# account: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/
NCBI_API_KEY=
# NCBI asks for a contact address on bulk requests.
NCBI_EMAIL=
# Where to cache PubMed searches and abstracts. Augmentation and the evidence check both read
# it, so a paper is fetched once; point it at a shared directory to share it across a team.
KGB_PUBMED_CACHE=data/cache/pubmed.sqlite
